{
 "_note": "Armory (spec v2 section 6): one weapon track per weapon. A track has tiers (4) of steps_per_tier purchases each; tier 1 step 0 is what everyone starts with. Each buy adds `step` to the tier's numbers; the steps_per_tier-th buy of a tier evolves the weapon to the next tier (new name, calibre, art and a stat jump); the last tier fills its bar and is then maxed. Purchase n (0-based over the whole track) costs cost.base x cost.growth^n, rounded like every price (economy.json price_round). Squad tracks multiply their owner's dmg and rate in LevelSim (upgrades.weapons), never troop counts. Bottle Shot tracks (owner finale_<weapon>) only change handling through `extra`: key <finale.json weapon key>_add adds, _mult multiplies (magazine, kick, draw, sway, steadiness); no aim assist. unlock_level = the level where the rank or the district's finale weapon first appears; before it the card is locked. Names are our own (no real brand or model; web-checked 2026-11-12); calibres are real. Prices are tuned by tests/econ_sim.gd.",
